## Summary
Two UN peacekeepers were killed and seven people injured in an ambush by unidentified gunmen during a patrol in South Sudan. The incident highlights the risks faced by peacekeeping forces in conflict-affected areas.

## Key Points
- Two UN peacekeepers were killed in the ambush.
- Seven people were injured during the attack.
- The attackers were unidentified gunmen.
- The incident occurred in South Sudan.
- It reflects ongoing violence and instability in the region.


